# Marketsynth Delivery Report (Cursor)

Use after implementation or audit tasks. **Do not** repeat full TZ. **Do not** claim PASS without evidence.

## DEFAULT IMPLEMENTATION REPORT

```
Verdict: PASS | FAIL | INCONCLUSIVE
Goal: [one line]
Changed files: [list]
Behavior change: before → after
Tests executed: [commands]
Results: [pass/fail counts or N/A]
Reviewer verdicts: [if composite review ran]
Limitations: [honest gaps]
Residual risks: [if any]
SoT updates: [files or none]
Next approved step: [single step from owner sequence]
```

## Rules

- No marketing language; no "foundation ready" without user-visible result (product tasks)
- PASS requires: scope met, required tests green (or N/A with reason), no unaddressed blocking review findings
- FAIL: blocking finding, failed verification, scope expansion, or unverified claims
- INCONCLUSIVE: missing files, env blocked verification, reviewers disagree on facts

## Composite review trigger

Run skill **marketsynth-composite-review** after **non-trivial code changes**:
- New/changed product logic, API, persistence, frontend flow, security-sensitive paths
- Before owner-facing PASS on product slices

**Do not run** composite review for: read-only Q&A, single-comment typo, pure governance doc edits.

Reviewers are **read-only** — they report findings; implementer fixes, then re-runs review.
